# Configured in fef-validation-common/application.properties
# validation.gherkin.scenario.parallelism: Scenarios per feature file run in parallel
# This uses Java ExecutorService (NOT Flink parallelism)
# Example: Feature file with 4 scenarios ? all 4 run concurrently in Java threads

# =====================================================
# ACTUAL PARALLELISM CALCULATION
# =====================================================
# Given:
# - 5 pipelines (processID/date combinations) picked at once
# - Each pipeline has 10 validations
# - Each feature has 4 scenarios
# - Flink cluster has N task slots
#
# Parallelism:
# 1. Main job: 5 TriggerProcessor instances (Flink parallelism=5)
# 2. Worker jobs: min(N task_slots, 5x10) = min(N, 50) jobs run concurrently
# 3. Scenarios: Each worker job runs 4 scenarios in parallel (Java threads)
#
# Maximum concurrent scenarios = min(N, 50) x 4
# - If N=50 task slots: 50 x 4 = 200 scenarios in parallel ?
# - If N=10 task slots: 10 x 4 = 40 scenarios in parallel
# - If N=100 task slots: 50 x 4 = 200 scenarios (limited by max-parallel=50)
# =====================================================
